/* Suspension, HOW TO TUNE:

Modes are in a MODES list.
Top-to-bottom order = mode1, mode2, mode3, etc.
You can toggle modes by name ("Race Mode") or by mode# ("mode1").

BH = wheel height when not turning.
Seconds    = how fast suspension transitions (lower = snappier).

Lean uses TWO caps:
LeanMaxDeltaOuter = max OUTSIDE wheel rise
LeanMaxDeltaInner = max INSIDE wheel drop

Lean is speed-scaled with multipliers (%):
LO_* = OUTER multiplier curve (Speed1->Mult1, Speed2->Mult2)
LI_* = INNER multiplier curve (Speed1->Mult1, Speed2->Mult2)
100 = full delta, 50 = half, 0 = no lean, 150 = 1.5x

StrengthFront/Middle/Rear = suspension strength per axle group.
HeightOffsetFront/Middle/Rear = extra height offset per axle group.

UseOwnSteer = true uses the mode's steering points below it,
false uses DEFAULT_*_STEER_POINTS at the top.

For making new modes, I recommend using my Chknese Imperial Nexus
html site, the Tuning Lab allows for more visual tuning :)
*/



/*
MODE LEGEND (quick reference):
BH/EH     = Base Height / End Height
HS/HE     = Height Start/End Speed (m/s)
Seconds   = Transition speed (lower = snappier)
LeanMax*  = Lean caps (meters)
LO_*      = Outer lean curve (speed -> percent)
LI_*      = Inner lean curve (speed -> percent)
OSA/OEA   = Outside strength additive start/end
OSS/OES   = Outside strength additive speed range (m/s)
UseOwnSteer = Use the mode's steering points (else defaults)
*/

